{"id": "sevt_011PHDtWEjbdxuTdMfJC5soB", "content": [{"text": "The checkout diff `6db1b9b` is the classic N+1: the old code ran one batched query (`order_id__in=ids`) then grouped in memory; the new loop runs a separate `OrderItem` query per order row. That's the top item on the \"burned us\" list (per-row query where there used to be a batch). The cart diff `50293ce` *adds* backoff (an improvement), and cart isn't the paged service \u2014 red herring. Let me confirm in the log.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:29:47.262336Z", "type": "agent.message"}
